For the equal-probability distribution $p_i=
\begin{cases}
1/n, & i\in\mathcal N,\\
0, & i\notin\mathcal N,
\end{cases}
\qquad |\mathcal N|=n,$ the general formula becomes $\begin{aligned}
S
&=-n\left(\frac1n\right)\log\left(\frac1n\right)\\
&=\log n.\end{aligned}$ It therefore reproduces the elementary counting definition. A distribution concentrated with certainty on one state has $S=0$.

